Fixed and committed.

**What broke (both in my uncommitted `src/help.rs` test addition):**

1. `routed_cli_subcommands_parses_arm_shapes — the fixture used a "...\n\ line-continued string literal. Rust's \` continuation strips leading whitespace on each continuation line, so the intended 12-space-indented `"health" => {` line arrived with zero indentation and the extractor (which keys on exactly 12 spaces) rejected it. Rebuilt the fixture as an explicit array of lines joined with \n, so indentation is literal and visible.

2. cli_help_documents_every_routed_subcommand — not a test bug. The new test correctly found that evolution and extended are routed in dispatch_sub.rs (lines 292 and 356) but absent from cli_help_text(). Added both to the --help subcommand list; extended's line states honestly that it only prints usage and needs an interactive session, which is what its dispatch arm actually does.

Verification: `cargo fmt, cargo build, cargo test (4558 + 89 pass, 0 failed), cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings clean. Confirmed the new lines render in real yoyo --help output. Committed as 2876065f`.
